      <p class="hot-eyebrow">Hanukkah · Friday evening, December 4, through Saturday, December 12</p>
      <h2>Hanukkah: eight nights, one small plate each</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="hot-lede">A dairy-and-fish table, already in the freezer: lox, bagels, cream cheese, cucumber, roe. Not eight dinners. One thing on the table each night, under the candles, that people can stand around.</p>
      <ul class="hot-hooks">
        <li>The color of the oil: beet-cured steelhead and salmon roe against a dark plate and a candle.</li>
        <li>Be honest about the fritters. They are a twist on the latke, not the tradition.</li>
        <li>Finish the eighth night with roe, on whatever is on the table.</li>
      </ul>
